{"type":"message","id":"fae137db","parentId":"2f8766a4","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:16:07.155Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-17 22:46 GMT+5:30] Implement the safest stability fixes from the root cause analysis, with backup and rollback.\n\n**Goal**: Improve gateway stability and reduce rate limit disruptions with minimal risk.\n\n**Safe fixes to apply (in order):**\n\n1. **WebSocket keepalive tuning** — add ping/pong intervals to prevent NAT timeouts\n   - Locate WebSocket server creation (likely in `dist/entry.js` or `src/ws-server.ts`)\n   - Set: `pingInterval: 30000`, `pingTimeout: 10000`\n   - This is low-risk and often helps\n\n2. **OpenRouter retry/backoff** — handle 429 responses gracefully\n   - Find OpenRouter provider code: `src/providers/openrouter.ts` or similar\n   - Add: detect 429, read `Retry-After` header, exponential backoff with jitter\n   - Also add config: `models.providers.openrouter.maxRetries: 3` and `backoffMs: 1000`\n   - This may require careful editing but is contained to one provider\n\n3. **Gateway lock cleanup** — make startup more robust\n   - Review lock handling code (likely `src/gateway/lock.ts` or similar)\n   - On startup, check if lock PID is still running; if not, auto-clear\n   - This prevents stale lock delays\n\n**Before making changes:**\n- Create a backup of the current config and affected source files\n- Document what will be changed and why\n- Prepare rollback steps (git revert or restore backups)\n\n**Regarding model backup/alternatives:**\n- Add `arcee-ai/trinity-large-preview:free` to the models catalog as a potential alternative\n- Update agent configs to include this as a fallback option (not switch primary yet)\n- This gives us a free backup model to test without disrupting current usage\n\n**Deliverables:**\n1. Summary of changes made\n2. File diffs or descriptions\n3. Verification steps to confirm fixes are working\n4. Any config updates needed to enable/disable features\n\n**Caution:** Only apply changes that are clearly reversible and well-understood. If any change requires complex modifications or could break running services, skip it and report why. Prioritize stability over completeness.\n\nWork in the OpenClaw project at `D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw`. Use your best judgment and be meticulous."}],"timestamp":1771348567152}}
